      <Placemark><name>Aiyari old airstrip</name><styleUrl>#closed</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>airstrip</b>, status: closed<br/>1 building(s) recorded<br/>Recorded in the field: "Aiyari's old airstrip was cleared in the early 1990s. Cone markers were put in place for landing, but no landing ever took place. Around 1993, one flight circled above the airstrip but never made its first landing. Airstrip is not in operation."]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.2184633,-9.3393317,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Awaru Old Airstrip</name><styleUrl>#closed</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>airstrip</b>, status: closed<br/>1 building(s) recorded<br/>Recorded in the field: "The soccer field at Awaru was cleared in the early 2000s as an airstrip. It was cleared after flights to Sila stopped due to a clan dispute between two brothers over the airstrip there. Once the dispute was resolved and flights resumed at Sila, the Awaru airstrip was abandoned and later houses were "]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.3886400,-9.0730017,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Old Dea Airstrip</name><styleUrl>#closed</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>airstrip</b>, status: closed<br/>1 building(s) recorded<br/>Recorded in the field: "The current location of Dea Primary School was formerly the old Dea airstrip. It became unusable due to excessive mud and a short runway, and no other flights landed after it was initially cleared. The original Dea School was established at Taparuraha, located between Dea, Ugunomo, and Siribu villag"]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.3268829,-9.0581295,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
